From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:40:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tvOS: template frameworks in the Xcode project

The Xcode project the tvOS export uses needs a place for the tvOS
template libraries, as it has for iOS and visionOS: the build's
generate_bundle step copies them into libgodot.tvos.debug.xcframework
and libgodot.tvos.release.xcframework, which upstream pull request
#118332 doesn't add, so tvOS templates couldn't be bundled at all.

These are the frameworks' Info.plist files and empty folders, as in
the tvos-port branch of sanarena/godot (closed pull request #123885).

Test: ./build.sh tvos ends with godot/bin/godot_tvos.zip, holding both
xcframeworks.

Upstream: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118332 (missing
there; worth suggesting on that pull request). Drop this patch with
the tvOS backport.
---
 .../Info.plist                                | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../tvos-arm64/empty                          |  1 +
 .../tvos-arm64_x86_64-simulator/empty         |  1 +
 .../Info.plist                                | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../tvos-arm64/empty                          |  1 +
 .../tvos-arm64_x86_64-simulator/empty         |  1 +
 6 files changed, 84 insertions(+)
